    "selectCount": 1,
    "domain": "Domain 1.0: Security Operations",
    "question": "The SOC receives a number of complaints regarding a recent uptick in desktop error messages that are associated with workstation access to an internal web application. An analyst, identifying a recently modified XML file on the web server, retrieves a copy of this file for review, which contains the following code:\n\nWhich of the following XML schema constraints would stop these desktop error messages from appearing?",
    "options": [
      "A. <pre class=\"font-mono\" style=\"margin:0; font-size:0.85rem; line-height:1.4;\">&lt;xs:element name=\"firstintro\"&gt;\n  &lt;xs:simpleType&gt;\n    &lt;xs:restriction base=\"xs:token\"&gt;\n      &lt;xs:pattern value=\"[0-9]{3}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{4}\"/&gt;\n    &lt;/xs:restriction&gt;\n  &lt;/xs:simpleType&gt;\n&lt;/xs:element&gt;</pre>",
      "B. <pre class=\"font-mono\" style=\"margin:0; font-size:0.85rem; line-height:1.4;\">&lt;xs:element name=\"firstintro\"&gt;\n  &lt;xs:simpleType&gt;\n    &lt;xs:restriction base=\"xs:positiveInteger\"&gt;\n      &lt;xs:pattern value=\"[0-9]\"/&gt;\n    &lt;/xs:restriction&gt;\n  &lt;/xs:simpleType&gt;\n&lt;/xs:element&gt;</pre>",
      "C. <pre class=\"font-mono\" style=\"margin:0; font-size:0.85rem; line-height:1.4;\">&lt;xs:element name=\"firstintro\"&gt;\n  &lt;xs:simpleType&gt;\n    &lt;xs:restriction base=\"xs:string\"&gt;\n      &lt;xs:pattern value=\"[a-zA-Z0-9]*\"/&gt;\n    &lt;/xs:restriction&gt;\n  &lt;/xs:simpleType&gt;\n&lt;/xs:element&gt;</pre>",
      "D. <pre class=\"font-mono\" style=\"margin:0; font-size:0.85rem; line-height:1.4;\">&lt;xs:element name=\"firstintro\"&gt;\n  &lt;xs:simpleType&gt;\n    &lt;xs:restriction base=\"xs:string\"&gt;\n      &lt;xs:pattern value=\"[0-9]*\"/&gt;\n    &lt;/xs:restriction&gt;\n  &lt;/xs:simpleType&gt;\n&lt;/xs:element&gt;</pre>"
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "explanation": "The modified XML file contains alphanumeric characters in the 'firstintro' element. Schema validation errors occur when values do not match the declared type or pattern constraints. Choice C defines a string restriction using the regex pattern '[a-zA-Z0-9]*', which permits any sequence of alphanumeric characters (both letters and numbers), resolving the validation mismatch and stopping desktop error messages.",
